{"id":"1e685079-e6db-43ee-a518-7dcc13e05be3","object":"chat.completion","created":1784883331,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Extract required fields\\n    try:\\n        initial_state = case['initial_state']\\n        max_steps = case['max_steps']\\n        tool_obs = case['tool_observations']\\n        transitions = case['transitions']\\n    except KeyError as e:\\n        raise ValueError(f'Missing required field: {e}')\\n    \\n    # Validate types\\n    if not isinstance(initial_state, str):\\n        raise ValueError('initial_state must be a string')\\n    if not isinstance(max_steps, int) or max_steps < 0:\\n        raise ValueError('max_steps must be a non-negative integer')\\n    if not isinstance(tool_obs, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('tool_observations must be a dict')\\n    if not isinstance(transitions, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('transitions must be a dict')\\n    \\n    current_state = initial_state\\n    step = 0\\n    trace = []\\n    final = None\\n    status = None\\n    \\n    # Helper to get state info\\n    def get_state(state_name):\\n        if state_name not in transitions:\\n            raise ValueError(f'State \\\"{state_name}\\\" not found in transitions')\\n        state_info = transitions[state_name]\\n        if not isinstance(state_info, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(f'State \\\"{state_name}\\\" info is not a dict')\\n        if 'kind' not in state_info:\\n            raise ValueError(f'State \\\"{state_name}\\\" missing \\\"kind\\\"')\\n        return state_info\\n    \\n    # Check if initial state is final before loop\\n    state_info = get_state(current_state)\\n    if state_info['kind'] == 'final':\\n        if 'value' not in state_info:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Final state \\\"{current_state}\\\" missing \\\"value\\\"')\\n        final = state_info['value']\\n        status = 'completed'\\n        return {'final': final, 'status': status, 'trace': trace}\\n    \\n    # Main loop bounded by max_steps\\n    while step < max_steps:\\n        state_info = get_state(current_state)\\n        if state_info['kind'] == 'final':\\n            if 'value' not in state_info:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Final state \\\"{current_state}\\\" missing \\\"value\\\"')\\n            final = state_info['value']\\n            status = 'completed'\\n            break\\n        elif state_info['kind'] == 'action':\\n            if 'action' not in state_info:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Action state \\\"{current_state}\\\" missing \\\"action\\\"')\\n            action = state_info['action']\\n            if not isinstance(action, str):\\n                raise ValueError('Action must be a string')\\n            if action not in tool_obs:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Tool \\\"{action}\\\" not found in tool_observations')\\n            observation = tool_obs[action]\\n            if not isinstance(observation, str):\\n                raise ValueError('Observation must be a string')\\n            # Determine next state\\n            next_by_obs = state_info.get('next_by_observation', {})\\n            default_next = state_info.get('default_next')\\n            if default_next is None:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Action state \\\"{current_state}\\\" missing \\\"default_next\\\"')\\n            next_state = next_by_obs.get(observation, default_next)\\n            if next_state not in transitions:\\n                raise ValueError(f'Next state \\\"{next_state}\\\" not in transitions')\\n            # Record trace\\n            trace.append({\\n                'step': step,\\n                'state': current_state,\\n                'action': action,\\n                'observation': observation\\n            })\\n            current_state = next_state\\n            step += 1\\n        else:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Invalid state kind \\\"{state_info[\\\"kind\\\"]}\\\" for state \\\"{current_state}\\\"')\\n    \\n    if status is None:\\n        status = 'max_steps'\\n        final = None\\n    \\n    return {'final': final, 'status': status, 'trace': trace}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) according to the specification. The case payload contains initial_state, max_steps, tool_observations (map from tool name to observation string), and transitions (map from state name to object with kind, action, next_by_observation, default_next). Also _case_nonce but not needed.\n\nWe need to simulate the ReAct loop: start at initial_state, for up to max_steps steps. Each step we look at current state. If state is final (kind \"final\"), we stop and set final to its value, status \"final\" (or similar? The output schema has \"final\" field which is string or null, and \"status\" which is string). In examples from task description: \"final\" likely the final value, \"status\" probably \"completed\" or \"failed\"? Actually output schema: final is null or string, status is string. From typical ReAct, status could be \"completed\" if reached final state, \"max_steps_reached\" if ran out of steps? Need to infer.\n\nLook at the task description: \"Stop on completion or max steps and return status, final value, and trace.\" The status likely indicates if final was reached or not. Possibly \"completed\" and \"max_steps_exceeded\"? But we must produce exactly JSON matching schema. The schema allows any string for status. We'll define status as \"completed\" if we reached a final state, else \"max_steps\" if we exceed max steps without reaching final. Also if invalid state or missing tool? The task says to raise ValueError for infeasible/structurally invalid case. So we validate inputs.\n\nThe trace: array of objects with step, action, observation, state. Each step: when we are in action state, we perform action (tool), get observation from tool_observations using the tool name. Then transition: check if observation is in next_by_observation, else use default_next. The new state becomes that. Record step number (starting from 0 or 1? In typical ReAct trace, maybe step counts each action. We'll start step=0 for first action. The output schema says step integer. We'll increment each action.\n\nWe also need to record state before action? The trace object has \"state\": string. Likely the current state before the action is taken. And \"observation\" the observation received after action. \"action\" the tool name. So for each step: current_state -> action (tool) -> observation -> next_state. Trace entry: step, state (current state), action, observation. Then update current state to next state.\n\nIf current state is final: we set final to its value, status \"completed\". No trace entry for final step? The specification: \"A final state terminates without a tool call.\" So we do not add a trace entry for final state itself. We just stop. The trace should include only action steps. The step count should be the number of actions performed. In max_steps constraints, if we run out of steps, we stop and status \"max_steps\" and final null? But if we reach final state within steps, we have final value and status completed. If we exceed max_steps without final, final is null and status \"max_steps\". But need to ensure step count <= max_steps? The loop: for step in range(max_steps): we take an action if current state is non-final. If after an action we get to final, next iteration will break. If after max_steps actions we are still in action state, we break and status max_steps.\n\nPotential edge case: initial state may be final. Then we should immediately stop with final value, no trace. Steps = 0.\n\nAlso validation: Ensure tool exists in tool_observations. Ensure state exists in transitions. Ensure kind is \"action\" or \"final\". For action state, action must be a string, next_by_observation may not contain the observation? Use default_next. Ensure default_next exists in transitions. If missing, it's infeasible -> ValueError.\n\nAlso tool_observations keys are tool names; if action not in tool_observations, raise ValueError? The task says \"invalid-action feedback\" but we need to decide: if tool not in tool_observations, we cannot get observation. Does that mean we should treat as invalid action? The description: \"Select the observation-specific successor or the default; distinguish missing tools and states.\" Possibly we should raise ValueError if tool is missing because it's invalid case. The specification says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case\". So if case payload has missing tool or missing state, it's invalid.\n\nAlso note that transitions may contain \"bad\" state etc. Ensure default_next string points to a valid state.\n\nImplementation steps:\n\n- Extract fields from case: initial_state, max_steps, tool_observations, transitions.\n- Validate they are present and correct types.\n- Initialize current_state = initial_state, step = 0, trace = [], final = None, status = None.\n- Loop while step < max_steps:\n    - Lookup current_state in transitions. If not present, raise ValueError.\n    - If transitions[current_state][\"kind\"] == \"final\":\n        - final = transitions[current_state][\"value\"] (should be string)\n        - status = \"completed\"\n        - break\n    - Else if kind == \"action\":\n        - action = transitions[current_state][\"action\"]\n        - if action not in tool_observations: raise ValueError\n        - observation = tool_observations[action]\n        - Get next_state from transitions[current_state][\"next_by_observation\"].get(observation, transitions[current_state][\"default_next\"])\n        - Ensure next_state in transitions: if not, raise ValueError? Actually default_next should be valid; but we can check.\n        - Append trace entry: {\"step\": step, \"state\": current_state, \"action\": action, \"observation\": observation}\n        - current_state = next_state\n        - step += 1\n    - else: raise ValueError (invalid kind)\n- After loop, if status is None (i.e., we didn't break due to final):\n    - status = \"max_steps\"\n    - final = None\n\nReturn {\"final\": final, \"status\": status, \"trace\": trace}\n\nNote: The output schema requires \"trace\" array with objects having step, action, observation, state. Ensure all keys present.\n\nAlso consider that max_steps may be 0? Then loop not entered. If initial_state is final, we should handle before loop? Actually loop condition step < max_steps, if max_steps=0, we skip loop. Then we need to check if initial state is final. So before loop, check if current_state is final: set status=completed, final=value, trace=[], return. Else if not final and max_steps=0, then we cannot proceed -> status max_steps? But max_steps=0 means no steps allowed, but if we are not final, we cannot do anything. According to bounded loop: max_steps bounds the number of actions. If max_steps=0 and initial_state not final, we cannot take any action, so it's effectively max_steps reached. So status = \"max_steps\", final null, trace empty.\n\nEdge cases: infinite loop detection? Not required, but we have max_steps bound.\n\nNow write Python code. Use standard library only. Must not mutate case input.\n\nAlso note: The candidate_artifact description says \"Implement react_tool_loop_controller through solve(case)\". The function name is solve(case). So define solve(case) that returns dict.\n\nWe need to produce JSON output with key \"implementation\" and value as string of Python source code.\n\nBe careful to escape newlines, quotes, backslashes in the JSON string.\n\nWe'll write code with proper indentation.\n\nLet's produce the solution."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1694,"completion_tokens":2597,"total_tokens":4291,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1644},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_